    "narrative": "For May 8, 2026, the Austin Waves look to capitalize on favorable matchups at the top and middle of the order. Our premier play today is **Jackson Merrill** (75.26), who draws a high-leverage start against McGreevy. His 10% bonus for leading off, combined with a significant platoon advantage against the right-handed McGreevy, cements his status as our primary engine for Runs and SB volume. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** (71.24) remains an elite start; while facing a left-hander in Lopez usually triggers a penalty, the park factors and his specific skill set\u2014paired with his high-upside spot in the #2 hole\u2014keep his efficiency well above the 70-point threshold. We are also closely tracking **Coby Mayo** (65.57), whose ability to exploit the platoon edge against Lopez makes him a high-efficiency target for power, despite the risk associated with facing a crafty arm.\n\nThe most difficult decision on our bench was bypassing **Miguel Vargas** (51.54). He hovered just outside our active rotation, narrowly edged out by **Brady House** (52.10) and **Josh Lowe** (53.09). While **Miguel Vargas** provided a balanced profile, the optimizer favored **Josh Lowe** specifically for his matchup against Cease; the aggressive 14% platoon boost and the expectation that Cease\u2019s slow delivery will permit a stolen base opportunity for **Josh Lowe** provided the tie-breaking edge. We must remain cautious, however, regarding the heavy exposure to elite arms like Sale; despite the status of **Kyle Tucker** (50.23) and **Andy Pages** (45.83), their raw projected efficiency is dampened by Sale\u2019s elite strikeout rate. Keep a close watch on **Drake Baldwin**, whose score of 46.80 sits near our marginal threshold; if defensive substitutions occur late in the game, we will look to preserve our caps by pivoting to our bench depth.",
